  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rExisting: 100_R1, 101_R1,120_R1,121_R1, 122_R1, 140_R1, 141_R1, 600_R1,601_R1\rProposed: 200_R2, 201_R2,220_R2, 221_R2,222_R2,240_R2, 241_R1\rHeritage, Design and access statement, dated 28.5.26\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that match the existing building or as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "Prior to the above groundwork of the reconstruction of the boundary wall, detailed drawings and specifications of the proposed boundary wall shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include:\r \roAmended drawings clearly confirming the gap between the new boundary wall and the main building;\r\roBrick type, colour, texture, bond;\r\roDetails of the coping, including materials, profile, dimensions, and method of construction;\r\roMortar mix, colour, texture, and pointing profile;\r\roDetails of the treatment of both terminating ends of the wall; \r\roDetails of the paving treatment;\r\roSamples of the materials to be used; and\r\roLarge-scale drawings of all relevant details and junctions.\r \rThe boundary wall shall thereafter be constructed in accordance with the approved details and retained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory external appearance with the conservation area. \r"
  ],
